Z||000000||RedHaze86SD4||11-21-2001||04:32 PM||||I'm working on some design ideas and one of my projects ended up becoming sorta rebody type. Anyways without giving too much detail on my "top secret" project  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I was wondering about peoples thoughts on mounting a headlight assembly directly to the metal bumper under the fascia!?!? Working in a new fascia design that uses dot approved headlights incorperated into the new fascia design... also.. besides 92-9? MR2 front blinkers, anyone have any suggestions for some nice looking ones that might work to mount flush and kinda wrap around the front some?  ok just curious.. Help if ya can. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/redhaze1_1.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||11-21-2001||04:44 PM||||for that kind of work.... best thing to do it visit all the new/used car lots and the salvage yards. Something's bound to turn up.<P>Whatever you mount the new lamp assembly to needs to be fairly stable and solid. Vibrating headlamps often won't last as long as they should and will make flikering light down the road that will be really straining when driving.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
